%description:

Tcp.pmtudEnabled:on -- DF and a Fragmentation Needed make host1 send smaller segments.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Path MTU Discovery (RFC 1191, RFC 1981) enabled/disabled".

The classes: on (true, the default) and off (false, the value of LegacyTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::sendToIP() sets DF on each IPv4 segment with true;
TcpConnection::processIcmpv4Error() reduces the MSS at a Fragmentation Needed and sends the
lost segment again. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, which sends 10000 bytes to host2 through the router, whose link to
host2 has an MTU of 1000 bytes; the segments of host1 carry 1500 bytes of IP. Observation: level 1, the first data frame that reaches host2 has DF and at most 1000 bytes
of IP: the router dropped the larger segment and sent a Fragmentation Needed.

%# parameter: Tcp.pmtudEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.pmtudEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPmtudEnabledOn")
        .once(on("host2.eth[0].mac").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.dontFragment == true && ipv4.totalLengthField <= 1000B && ipv4.moreFragments == false")
                  .describe("the first data frame at host2")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPmtudEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.pmtudEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.router.eth[1].mac.mtu = 1000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPmtudEnabledOn: PASS
